    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d157-a1">

                <pb facs="0325" n="229" sameAs="frus:frus1898/pg229"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in No. 61.]</seg></opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Tsung-li Yamên to Mr.
                            Conger.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1898-10-04"><hi rendition="#italic">October 4,
                        1898</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 17.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Your Excellency</hi>: The prince and ministers have
                    the honor to inform your excellency that on the 4th instant the grand council
                    memorialized the Throne that in the several localities of the live districts of
                    Peking there are both good and bad men, and the other day some foreigners were
                    on their way from the railway station <pb facs="0326" n="230" xml:id="pg230"/>
                    and were set upon by a mob. The gendarmerie have been commanded and have already
                    appointed over 100 soldiers to guard the road from the station to the Yung-ting
                    gate and up to the T’ien bridge, and to keep a sharp lookout to arrest offenders
                    and preserve the peace. All the police stations within and without the city are
                    commanded to protect foreigners who may be passing, and they shall not be
                    delayed.</p>
                <p>On the same day the censors were likewise ordered by the imperial decree to guard
                    the road from the station, etc. (same as above).</p>
                <p>This yamen has therefore ordered the gendarmerie and censors to obey the imperial
                    mandate and take the necessary measures.</p>
                <p>In addition, as in duty bound, we forward the above copy of the decree for your
                    excellency’s information.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
